  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "dfd7dbf4-e30e-40fa-ab07-404e2edad0a9",
    "name": "Sentera FieldAgent GraphQL API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "The Sentera FieldAgent API is a GraphQL API, not a resource-oriented REST API. All operations - queries and mutations covering fields, surveys, flight tasks, imagery, mosaics, analytics, orders, and organizations - are sent as GraphQL documents to a single HTTP endpoint (https://api.sentera.com/graphql) using POST (GET is also supported).\nBecause there are no per-resource REST paths to enumerate, this OpenAPI document models only the one real HTTP transport endpoint that fronts the GraphQL schema. The full operation catalog (30+ queries such as `field`, `fields`, `survey`, `surveys`, `task`, `tasks`, `analytic`, `order`, `orders`, `organization`, and 80+ mutations such as `create_field`, `place_order`, and webhook subscriptions) is defined by the GraphQL schema rather than by HTTP paths; see graphql/sentera-graphql.md and the upstream GraphQL reference at https://api.sentera.com/api/docs/operation/query/index.html.\nNo fabricated REST endpoints are included.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Sentera Support",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
